{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nplan={\\\"description\\\":\\\"Discriminator: after a recovery commits the instance holding an admitted client operation as NOOP, does the owner's re-proposal carry the operation all the way to a client reply? Prefix: the harness admits the operation with the real client-proposal handler, delivers the NOOP commit, drains the re-proposed operation from the propose channel, runs the normal PreAccept/commit rounds with a peer through the real codec, and then applies the re-proposed instance with the real executor. Controls: the events print the pending count before the commit, whether a re-proposal appeared on the channel, the new instance's status at both replicas, and the bytes written to the client's reply writer.\\\",\n \\\"claim_id\\\":\\\"C5-noop-commit-reproposes-admitted-operation\\\",\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB6-repropose\\\"],\n \\\"harness\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"go_test\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"In-package Go test that drives admit, NOOP commit, re-propose, commit of the re-proposed instance and execution, reporting the client's reply bytes.\\\",\n  \\\"semantic_changes\\\":[\\\"harness-only scaffolding: two Replica values are constructed in-package with buffer peer writers; the handlers are unmodified and messages travel through the real codec\\\",\\\"the client's reply writer is a harness buffer, so the observation is the bytes the implementation wrote\\\"],\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admitted\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"operation_admitted\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"pending\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}]}],\n  \\\"legality\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S13-handleCommit\\\",\\\"S8-handlePropose-startPhase1\\\",\\\"S12-handleAcceptReply\\\",\\\"S20-exec\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB6-repropose\\\"],\n   \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"Every step is the implementation's own: the client-proposal handler, the commit handler's re-proposal branch, the pre-accept and commit rounds, and the executor that answers the client.\\\",\\\"applicability\\\":\\\"Owner-alive case, one operation, N=3 Thrifty.\\\",\\\"unresolved\\\":[\\\"the peer is a second harness replica rather than a separately configured participant\\\"],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]}},\n \\\"monitors\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"M1-client-reply\\\",\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH2-client-reply\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"client_reply_after_recovery\\\",\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB6-repropose\\\"],\n   \\\"grounding\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S12-handleAcceptReply\\\",\\\"S20-exec\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB6-repropose\\\"],\n    \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"The event reports whether the re-proposed instance executed and how many bytes reached the client's writer, which is the completion the client contract needs.\\\",\\\"applicability\\\":\\\"The operation was admitted and re-proposed, and the re-proposed instance committed.\\\",\\\"unresolved\\\":[],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"instance\\\",\\\"reference\\\":\\\"admitted.instance\\\"}],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admitted\\\"}],\n \\\"observable_properties\\\":[{\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH2-client-reply\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"event_assertion\\\",\\\"trigger\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"event\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"client_reply_after_recovery\\\"},\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"replied\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"instance\\\"],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"An operation that a NOOP recovery forced the owner to re-propose must still be answered on the client's connection.\\\"}],\n \\\"uncertainties\\\":[\\\"the harness supplies the client's reply writer, so it observes the bytes the implementation wrote rather than a socket\\\",\\\"one operation and one re-proposal round are exercised\\\"]}\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"check\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"unit-C5-noop-commit-reproposes-admitted-operation\\\",\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Second scenario for the same protection, closing the limitation that the first check stopped at the propose channel: this harness carries the re-proposed operation through the normal PreAccept and commit rounds with a peer via the real codec, commits the new instance at both replicas, applies it with the real executor and observes the client's reply. The local construction run shows pending 1 before the commit, a re-proposal on the channel after it, the new instance committed at both replicas, and execution writing 17 bytes to the client's writer (replied true) - so the operation survives a NOOP recovery end to end. The obligation, plan predicates and binding are the reviewed ones; the trusted runner and a fresh correspondence review decide the formal outcome.\\\",\n \\\"plan_path\\\":\\\"plan-client-reply.json\\\",\\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"explore_client_reply2_test.go\\\",\\\"files\\\":{}}\njson.dump(plan,open('plan-client-reply.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-client-reply.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('written')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-client-reply.json 2>&1 | head -6\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
